  "tutorialStart": "Get started",
  "tutorialWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to KeepInventory",
  "tutorialWelcomeBody": "Your inventory and till on your phone, fully offline. Everything is in the side menu: Selling, Catalog and Data. Here are the basics in one minute.",
  "tutorialInventoryTitle": "1. Add your products",
  "tutorialInventoryBody": "In Inventory tap + and enter name, price, cost and units; you'll see your margin right away. Optionally group products by category (🏷️ button at the top). To tweak, tap − / + or the value itself. To change several at once, long-press a product and choose Edit.",
  "tutorialOffersTitle": "2. Offers and packs",
  "tutorialOffersBody": "In Offers create promotions (10% off, 3 for €12…) and combos (T-shirt + cap = €20, or any product of a category). They apply automatically when selling. From a promotion's ⋮ menu you can set it on a whole category. In Packs group products with their own price.",
  "tutorialSalesTitle": "3. Sell in seconds",
  "tutorialSalesBody": "In Checkout tap products to add them to the cart, press CHARGE and choose how the customer pays. The 🏷️ tag on each line gives a one-off discount (%, € or final price). If something is missing to complete a combo, the cart tells you: tap the notice to go to the product or ＋ Add to put it in. If you leave the checkout, the cart is kept.",
  "tutorialHistoryTitle": "4. Tickets and fairs",
  "tutorialHistoryBody": "In Tickets and fairs you have the ticket of every sale. Group a fair's days with the fair button (fairs are kept for next time). From a ticket you can refund units and the amount is recalculated with the offers; lines with a manual discount can't be refunded. A fully refunded ticket stays as Refunded.",
  "tutorialDashboardTitle": "5. Balance the till",
  "tutorialDashboardBody": "Home shows revenue, profit and what was paid with each method. Perfect for balancing the till at the end of the day.",
  "tutorialDataTitle": "7. Your data, safe",
  "tutorialDataBody": "In Backups and sync back up your data or move everything to another phone with a QR code, no Wi‑Fi needed (both phones must have the same app version). You can replay this tutorial from the menu, under Help.",
